\ Test polymorphic fixnum/float arithmetic in AOT compiled code.
\ User-defined words receive parameters as raw_at_slot, triggering
\ the polymorphic tag-check branching path.
\
\ In AOT mode bail is fatal, so correct output proves no bail occurred.

add:  ( a b -- c ) [ + ] ;
sub:  ( a b -- c ) [ - ] ;
mul:  ( a b -- c ) [ * ] ;
fdiv: ( a b -- c ) [ / ] ;
mod:  ( a b -- c ) [ % ] ;

\ === Addition: all four type combinations ===
3 2.5 add .
2.5 3 add .
3 3 add .
2.5 1.5 add .

\ === Subtraction: all four type combinations ===
10 2.5 sub .
10.0 3 sub .
5 3 sub .
4.5 1.5 sub .

\ === Multiplication: all four type combinations ===
4 2.5 mul .
2.5 4 mul .
3 3 mul .
2.5 1.5 mul .

\ === Division: all four type combinations ===
7 2.0 fdiv .
7.0 2 fdiv .
6 3 fdiv .
7.5 2.5 fdiv .

\ === Modulo: all four type combinations ===
7 2.0 mod .
7.0 2 mod .
7 3 mod .
7.5 2.0 mod .

\ === Edge cases: zero operands ===
0 2.5 add .
3.0 0 mul .

\ === Edge cases: negative mixed ===
-3 2.5 add .
4 -1.5 mul .
-7 3 mod .

\ === Edge cases: integer-valued floats ===
3.0 2 add .
2 3.0 sub .
